1623:"It's okay. Just take my hand."
1624:Words overflowing with love and encouragement surface from the depths of her memory.
1625:The warmth of their time together breaks through the fear in her heart, like sunlight cutting through dark clouds.
1626:A fierce, burning strength, unlike anything she'd ever felt, surges up from deep within.
1627:With trembling hands, Reina tries to push herself up from the armrests.
1628:She slams onto the cold, muddy ground.//nHer legs, still weak, buckle uselessly beneath her.
